<article class="env-definition" id="063S">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/063S">Definition <span data-tag="063S">31.23.2</span>.</a> Let $f : X \to S$ be a morphism of schemes. Let $i : Z \to X$ be an immersion. </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
We say $i$ is a <em>relative quasi-regular immersion</em> if $Z \to S$ is flat and $i$ is a quasi-regular immersion. 
</p>
</li><li><p>
We say $i$ is a <em>relative $H_1$-regular immersion</em> if $Z \to S$ is flat and $i$ is an $H_1$-regular immersion. 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
</article>